{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% block head %}
    <script src="/static/js/region-guess.js"></script>
    <style>
    .nt-cl h4 { margin-top: 2rem; }
    .nt-cl ol li { margin-bottom: .35rem; }
    .nt-cl .nt-url { display: flex; gap: .5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: .4rem 0 .2rem; }
    .nt-cl .nt-url code { font-size: .95rem; word-break: break-all; }
    .nt-cl .nt-note { font-size: .88rem; opacity: .75; }
    .nt-cl figure.nt-shots { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .8rem; align-items: flex-start; margin: .6rem 0 1rem; }
    .nt-cl figure.nt-shots img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, .5); border-radius: 6px; }
    .nt-cl figure.nt-shots figcaption { flex-basis: 100%; font-size: .82rem; opacity: .7; }
    .nt-cl kbd { font-size: .8em; }
    .nt-cl pre { background: rgba(127, 127, 127, .12); padding: .6rem .8rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: .82rem; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
    </style>
{% endblock head %}
{% block body %}
<div class="container nt-cl" style="max-width: 900px">
    <h2>Use the trackers in your torrent client</h2>
    <p>More trackers means more peers and faster downloads, especially for older or less popular torrents.
       The best way is to give your client this site's list <b>as a link</b>, so it stays up to date by itself.</p>

    <p class="nt-note">Each client below has screenshots with the settings marked &#9312;&#9313;&#9314;, matching the steps. Tap one to see it full size.</p>

    <p class="mb-0"><b>Your list</b> (working trackers, fast from <span id="nt-where">anywhere</span>):</p>
    <div class="nt-url"><code id="nt-list">https://newtrackon.co.nz/api/clean</code>
        <button id="nt-copy" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Copy</button></div>
    <p class="nt-note">For a different region or other options, see the <a href="/list">List</a> page.</p>

    <h4 id="qbittorrent">qBittorrent</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>Open <b>Tools &rarr; Preferences</b> (<kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>). Older versions call it <b>Options</b>; on a Mac it's <b>qBittorrent &rarr; Preferences</b>.</li>
        <li>Pick the <b>BitTorrent</b> page.</li>
        <li>Scroll down, tick <b>Automatically append trackers from URL to new downloads</b>, paste your list link into <b>URL</b>, and click <b>OK</b>.
            New torrents get the trackers from then on, and the list stays up to date.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="nt-shots">
        <a href="/static/img/clients/qbittorrent-1.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/qbittorrent-1.png" width="401" height="141" loading="lazy" alt="qBittorrent: Tools menu, Preferences"></a>
        <a href="/static/img/clients/qbittorrent-2.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/qbittorrent-2.png" width="803" height="617" loading="lazy" alt="qBittorrent Preferences, BitTorrent page: Automatically append trackers from URL to new downloads, with the list link in URL"></a>
        <figcaption>qBittorrent 5.1 on Linux; Windows looks the same.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="nt-note">No URL option in your version? Tick <b>Automatically append these trackers to new downloads</b> (just above it) instead
       and paste the list itself (open the link, copy everything). That copy won't update, so redo it now and then.
       Torrents added from the command line while qBittorrent isn't running don't get the URL trackers.</p>

    <h4 id="transmission">Transmission (4.0 or later)</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>Open <b>Edit &rarr; Preferences</b>.</li>
        <li>Pick the <b>Network</b> tab.</li>
        <li>Open your list link, copy everything, paste it into <b>Default Public Trackers</b>, and click <b>Close</b>.
            Transmission adds them to every public torrent.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="nt-shots">
        <a href="/static/img/clients/transmission-1.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/transmission-1.png" width="284" height="164" loading="lazy" alt="Transmission: Edit menu, Preferences"></a>
        <a href="/static/img/clients/transmission-2.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/transmission-2.png" width="665" height="695" loading="lazy" alt="Transmission Preferences, Network tab: Default Public Trackers filled in"></a>
        <figcaption>Transmission 4.1 on Linux. The Mac app doesn't have this box.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="nt-note">A pasted list doesn't update by itself: paste a fresh copy now and then. Running the daemon or the
       command-line version? The same setting is <code>"default-trackers"</code> in <code>settings.json</code> (stop Transmission first,
       and separate the trackers with <code>\n\n</code> typed inside the quotes).</p>

    <h4 id="deluge">Deluge</h4>
    <p>Deluge can't do it on its own, but the <a href="https://github.com/stefantalpalaru/deluge-default-trackers">Default Trackers</a>
       plugin can: it adds trackers to new public torrents (never to private ones) and reloads them from a link.</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Install the plugin: <b>Edit &rarr; Preferences &rarr; Plugins &rarr; Install</b> (pick the file built for your Deluge's Python version),
            then tick <b>DefaultTrackers</b>.</li>
        <li>A <b>Default Trackers</b> page appears: pick it.</li>
        <li>Paste your list link into <b>tracker list URL</b> (it reloads every day) and click <b>OK</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="nt-shots">
        <a href="/static/img/clients/deluge-1.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/deluge-1.png" width="494" height="324" loading="lazy" alt="Deluge Preferences, Plugins: DefaultTrackers ticked"></a>
        <a href="/static/img/clients/deluge-2.png"><img src="/static/img/clients/deluge-2.png" width="784" height="304" loading="lazy" alt="Deluge Preferences, Default Trackers page: tracker list URL filled in"></a>
        <figcaption>Deluge 2.2 on Linux with Default Trackers 0.7.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h4 id="other">Any other client, or one download</h4>
    <p>Most clients let you add trackers to a torrent in its properties or <b>Trackers</b> tab: paste the list there.
       Or use <a href="/tools">Tools</a>: paste a magnet link or open a .torrent file, and get it back with the best trackers added.</p>

    <h4>Private trackers</h4>
    <p>Don't add public trackers to torrents from a private tracker: it's against their rules and can get your account banned.
       qBittorrent, Transmission and the Deluge plugin all leave private torrents alone, and so do the Tools here.</p>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
    var r = typeof ntGuessRegion === 'function' ? ntGuessRegion() : '';
    var url = 'https://newtrackon.co.nz/api/clean' + (r ? '?fast_from=' + r : '');
    document.getElementById('nt-list').textContent = url;
    if (r && typeof NT_REGION_NAMES !== 'undefined') { document.getElementById('nt-where').textContent = NT_REGION_NAMES[r]; }
    document.getElementById('nt-copy').addEventListener('click', function () {
        var b = this;
        (navigator.clipboard ? navigator.clipboard.writeText(url) : Promise.reject()).then(function () { b.textContent = 'Copied'; },
            function () { b.textContent = 'Select and copy it'; });
    });
})();
</script>
{% endblock %}
